{"parentUuid":"ef379d8e-94b7-4e84-8dc9-c4084c900496","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cd5Ai2gqcnMnS9QgAtWcz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ErGHPmonkdb8rmko8MwDyG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research AI agent adoption narratives","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are doing deep market research for a Hebrew-speaking founder. Output in HEBREW.\n\nCONTEXT: We are building a product where every employee in an organization gets a personal conversational AI agent (in their WhatsApp/Telegram) that walks them one-on-one through ADOPTING a change — a new system, tool, process, or methodology. This is NOT new-hire onboarding. It is change adoption for EXISTING employees. The founder's belief: the differentiation is NOT in the product or technology — it is in the STORY and NARRATIVE. So your research must focus on NARRATIVE, not feature lists.\n\nYOUR TASK — research this category and map the NARRATIVES:\nFind companies/products in these adjacent spaces (2025-2026, use web search heavily):\n1. AI agents / AI copilots for software adoption and enterprise change (e.g. WalkMe, Whatfix, Pendo and any AI-agent features they launched; newer AI-native adoption startups).\n2. AI agents for employee enablement, training, and \"adoption in the flow of work\".\n3. Any startup explicitly using the words \"agent\" + \"adoption\" or \"agent\" + \"onboarding\" for CHANGE (not new hires).\n\nFor EACH notable company/product, capture:\n- Name + one line of what it actually is + URL.\n- Its NARRATIVE: the exact hero headline / tagline / positioning line they use on their homepage (quote it verbatim if you can find it), and the STORY they tell (what problem-villain-hero frame, what emotional or strategic angle). I care about the words and the story, not the feature list.\n- Who they talk to (buyer: L&D? IT? CIO? ops?).\n\nThen write a NARRATIVE-PATTERN ANALYSIS: what are the 3-5 dominant story frames in this space (e.g. \"adoption is a data/analytics problem\", \"guidance overlay on the screen\", \"reduce time-to-productivity\", \"AI does the busywork\")? Which narratives are crowded/taken? Where is the white space — a story nobody is telling?\n\nBe concrete and quote real copy. Return well-structured Hebrew markdown. Do not pad. Prioritize the NARRATIVE dimension above all."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":63257,"output_tokens":2842,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2842,"cache_read_input_tokens":63257,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cd5Ai14MukYaFzM5NnSpq","attributionMcpServer":"nanoclaw","attributionMcpTool":"send_message","type":"assistant","uuid":"87a2cb05-5565-4fff-8099-3b11f7684e10","timestamp":"2026-07-16T05:16:48.152Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"daa15cef-d4ca-4e78-bec1-8958fa2eaa50","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"mutable-herding-clarke"}
{"parentUuid":"87a2cb05-5565-4fff-8099-3b11f7684e10","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cd5Ai2gqcnMnS9QgAtWcz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GenPPTaRZmrBghXTJxmuok","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research change management narratives","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are doing deep market research for a Hebrew-speaking founder. Output in HEBREW.\n\nCONTEXT: We are building a product where every employee gets a personal conversational AI agent that walks them one-on-one through ADOPTING a change (a new system, tool, process, or methodology) inside an existing organization. The founder's core belief: \"AI adoption is mostly not about AI — it's change management.\" He believes the differentiation is NOT the product/technology, it is the STORY and NARRATIVE. Your research must focus on NARRATIVE.\n\nYOUR TASK — map how the CHANGE-MANAGEMENT and ADOPTION world tells its story:\nUse web search heavily (2025-2026 sources). Cover:\n1. Classic change-management players and frameworks and their narrative: Prosci/ADKAR, Kotter, McKinsey change practice, big-4 adoption/change consulting. How do they FRAME adoption? What is their story and language?\n2. The \"human side of change\" / \"people not tech\" narrative — who owns it, what words do they use.\n3. Implementation partners / consultants who \"come to a project and leave\" (the temporary change-agent model): how do system-implementation and adoption consultancies position themselves narratively?\n4. Employee enablement / L&D adoption narratives (Enboarder, 360Learning, Leena AI etc.) — the STORY they tell to L&D and HR buyers.\n\nFor EACH, capture: name + what it is + URL + the NARRATIVE (verbatim tagline/positioning if findable + the story frame + the emotional/strategic angle + who they talk to).\n\nThen write a NARRATIVE-PATTERN ANALYSIS: what are the dominant story frames in change management/adoption (e.g. \"manage resistance\", \"align stakeholders\", \"structured methodology\", \"measure adoption\")? Which are crowded? Where is the narrative white space — especially a story that centers the INDIVIDUAL employee getting a personal companion through change, that nobody is telling well?\n\nBe concrete, quote real copy, structured Hebrew markdown, no padding. NARRATIVE above all."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":63257,"output_tokens":2842,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2842,"cache_read_input_tokens":63257,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cd5Ai14MukYaFzM5NnSpq","attributionMcpServer":"nanoclaw","attributionMcpTool":"send_message","type":"assistant","uuid":"82095d61-fc51-40d2-85bf-867ae6066131","timestamp":"2026-07-16T05:16:58.645Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"daa15cef-d4ca-4e78-bec1-8958fa2eaa50","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"mutable-herding-clarke"}
