ption is mostly not about AI — it's change management.\" He believes the differentiation is NOT the product/technology, it is the STORY and NARRATIVE. Your research must focus on NARRATIVE.\n\nYOUR TASK — map how the CHANGE-MANAGEMENT and ADOPTION world tells its story:\nUse web search heavily (2025-2026 sources). Cover:\n1. Classic change-management players and frameworks and their narrative: Prosci/ADKAR, Kotter, McKinsey change practice, big-4 adoption/change consulting. How do they FRAME adoption? What is their story and language?\n2. The \"human side of change\" / \"people not tech\" narrative — who owns it, what words do they use.\n3. Implementation partners / consultants who \"come to a project and leave\" (the temporary change-agent model): how do system-implementation and adoption consultancies position themselves narratively?\n4. Employee enablement / L&D adoption narratives (Enboarder, 360Learning, Leena AI etc.) — the STORY they tell to L&D and HR buyers.\n\nFor EACH, capture: name + what it is + URL + the NARRATIVE (verbatim tagline/positioning if findable + the story frame + the emotional/strategic angle + who they talk to).\n\nThen write a NARRATIVE-PATTERN ANALYSIS: what are the dominant story frames in change management/adoption (e.g. \"manage resistance\", \"align stakeholders\", \"structured methodology\", \"measure adoption\")? Which are crowded? Where is the narrative white space — especially a story that centers the INDIVIDUAL employee getting a personal companion through change, that nobody is telling well?\n\nBe concrete, quote real copy, structured Hebrew markdown, no padding. NARRATIVE above all.","agentId":"a976807d62e184c7d","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"מחקר העומק הושלם ונמסר לאליה — קובץ מלא בעברית + תקציר.\n\nמה שנמסר:\n- **מפה מלאה של 4 המחנות** עם URLs וציטוטים מילוליים: (1) השחקנים הקלאסיים — Prosci/ADKAR, Kotter, McKinsey, Big-4; (2) נרטיב \"הצד האנושי\" ב-AI adoption; (3) מטמיעים/יועצים + DAPs + h